33:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":"Source: WordStream 2026 Google Ads Benchmarks - 13,000+ search campaigns, April 2025 to March 2026. Unit: search-campaign conversion rate averages, not single-page rates."}]
34:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Why the widely-cited 2.35% figure is the wrong benchmark"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The 2.35% figure circulates widely as “the average landing page conversion rate.” It originates from a 2012 Unbounce dataset reproduced in a 2014 blog post. Using a 12-year-old figure as a current benchmark for paid search performance is not informative - the traffic landscape, mobile adoption rates, and advertising platform sophistication have all changed substantially."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"More importantly, the 2.35% figure was an all-traffic median - mixing organic, direct, email, and paid together. Paid search conversion rates are structurally higher than that figure because paid search visitors arrive with explicit purchase intent. The correct comparison for a paid search landing page is the WordStream 2026 data above, not a 2012 all-traffic median."}]]}]
35:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Traffic source is the largest variable"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Traffic source determines how warm and how intent-qualified the visitor is when they land. The same page with the same offer can show dramatically different rates by source."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-4","children":[["$","li","Paid search (Google Ads)",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Paid search (Google Ads)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Highest intent of the paid channels. Visitor was actively searching for a solution. WordStream 2026 all-industries average: 8.18%. Use vertical-specific figures for comparison."}]]}],["$","li","Paid social (Meta, TikTok, LinkedIn)",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Paid social (Meta, TikTok, LinkedIn)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Interruption traffic - the visitor was not searching for your offer. Conversion rates are structurally lower. Comparing paid social rates against the WordStream paid search benchmark will always make your page look underperforming."}]]}],["$","li","Email (owned list)",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Email (owned list)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Warmest traffic type. Visitors already trust the sender. Email traffic to a landing page commonly converts at 2–5x the rate of cold paid traffic on the same page."}]]}],["$","li","Retargeting",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Retargeting"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Visitor has already seen your brand or page. Higher conversion rate than cold traffic from the same channel by design - this is the expected retargeting premium, not a page quality signal."}]]}]]}]]}]
36:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"How to use benchmarks as a diagnostic tool, not a verdict"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A conversion rate below the vertical benchmark is a signal that something is broken - not a conclusion about which thing is broken or how bad it is. The right response to a low rate is to run a signal-level diagnosis:"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-3","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[1,"."]}],"Segment by source and device - confirm the low rate is present on the channel you are optimising for, not an artefact of a high-bounce source dragging the overall number down."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[2,"."]}],"Check load time - if LCP is above 4 seconds on mobile, fix that before anything else. You cannot diagnose copy or layout problems if visitors are bouncing before the page renders."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[3,"."]}],"Run the 9-signal check - message-match, trust, mobile layout, load time, CTA clarity, form friction, proof. The first broken signal is the first fix. Earlier signals gate later ones."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-bold text-accent","children":[4,"."]}],"Compare against the right benchmark - your vertical, your traffic source, your offer type. A B2B SaaS lead-gen page at 4% compared against an e-commerce transaction benchmark is a category error."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"You need at least 500 paid traffic sessions to a single page before your conversion rate is statistically meaningful. Below that, a single unusual week can shift a 3% rate to 8% and back without the page changing. Focus on structural signal checks before optimising toward a number."}]]}]
37:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Frequently asked questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What is a good landing page conversion rate?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"It depends on traffic source, offer type, and vertical. For paid search (Google Ads), WordStream's 2026 benchmarks across 13,000+ campaigns found an all-industries average of 8.18%. For Business Services - the most relevant vertical for B2B lead gen - the average is 4.85%. A rate below your vertical's average with meaningful traffic (500+ sessions) is a diagnostic signal, not a verdict. The right question is not 'is my rate good' but 'which of the 9 conversion signals is pulling it down.'"}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"Are conversion rate benchmarks comparable across industries?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"No, and comparing across verticals is one of the most common benchmarking mistakes. WordStream's 2026 Google Ads data shows conversion rates ranging from 2.64% in Finance and Insurance to 16.22% in Animals and Pets - a 6x gap. A 3% conversion rate is below average for an Automotive Repair shop but above average for a Finance lead generation page. Always compare against your own vertical's benchmark, not an all-industries figure."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"Does traffic source affect conversion rate?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Yes, significantly. Paid search traffic (Google Ads) arrives with higher intent than paid social traffic (Meta, TikTok) - the visitor was actively searching for a solution, not interrupted while scrolling. Email list traffic is warmer than either. This means the same page can show 1% from cold paid social, 5% from paid search, and 12% from a warm email list. Benchmarking your page's overall rate against paid-search averages when your traffic mix is primarily cold social will make your page look worse than it is."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What conversion rate should I aim for on a landing page?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Compare your page with a documented benchmark segmented by vertical, traffic source, offer, and conversion action. Treat the benchmark as context, not a diagnosis: performance differences can come from the ad, audience, offer, measurement, or page. Use the page signals to form testable hypotheses rather than treating one benchmark number as the cause."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How many sessions do I need before my conversion rate is meaningful?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"At least 500 paid traffic sessions to a single landing page before drawing diagnostic conclusions. Below that, variance is too high - a single week with unusual traffic composition can shift a 3% rate to 8% and back without the page changing at all. If you are below 500 sessions, focus on ensuring the 9 signals are in place structurally rather than optimising toward a number."}]]}],"$L3c","$L3d","$L3e"]}]]}]
38:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-accent/40 bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Find what is pulling your rate down"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The free Nebula audit identifies likely page-side leaks. The $97 One-Leak Repair Sprint delivers a tailored kit for one high-confidence page-level finding. You or your developer implements it, and the 30-day re-audit verifies the page condition. It does not promise conversion lift."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-4","children":[["$","$L21",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre&utm_medium=organic-content","className":"inline-flex rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-bg hover:opacity-85 hover:bg-accent transition-colors","children":"Run the free audit"}],["$","$L21",null,{"href":"/pricing","className":"inline-flex rounded border border-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-accent hover:bg-accent-dim transition-colors","children":"See the One-Leak Repair Sprint"}]]}]]}]
39:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Related leak checks"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-1","children":[["$","$L21","/learning-centre/landing-page-not-converting",{"href":"/learning-centre/landing-page-not-converting","className":"block border-b border-border py-2.5 text-fg-muted transition-colors last:border-0 hover:text-accent","children":"Landing Page Not Converting? Diagnose These 5 Leaks First"}],["$","$L21","/learning-centre/google-ads-clicks-no-sales",{"href":"/learning-centre/google-ads-clicks-no-sales","className":"block border-b border-border py-2.5 text-fg-muted transition-colors last:border-0 hover:text-accent","children":"Google Ads Clicks But No Sales: Check The Page"}],["$","$L21","/learning-centre/high-cpc-low-conversion",{"href":"/learning-centre/high-cpc-low-conversion","className":"block border-b border-border py-2.5 text-fg-muted transition-colors last:border-0 hover:text-accent","children":"High CPC, Low Conversion: Which Layer Is Broken"}],["$","$L21","/learning-centre/landing-page-bounce-rate-high",{"href":"/learning-centre/landing-page-bounce-rate-high","className":"block border-b border-border py-2.5 text-fg-muted transition-colors last:border-0 hover:text-accent","children":"Landing Page Bounce Rate High: 3 Diagnosable Causes"}],["$","$L21","/learning-centre/before-you-raise-ad-budget",{"href":"/learning-centre/before-you-raise-ad-budget","className":"block border-b border-border py-2.5 text-fg-muted transition-colors last:border-0 hover:text-accent","children":"Before You Raise Ad Budget: Check These Landing Page Leaks"}]]}]]}]
3c:["$","div","5",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How do you calculate landing page conversion rate?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Divide completed conversions by total visitors, then multiply by 100. Example: 50 conversions ÷ 2,000 visitors × 100 = 2.5% conversion rate. Ensure your analytics platform correctly attributes all conversions to the landing page-partial page views or bot traffic can skew results."}]]}]
3d:["$","div","6",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What's the difference between mobile and desktop landing page conversion rates?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Mobile typically converts 20-40% lower than desktop, though this varies by industry and offer type. E-commerce often shows the largest gap; B2B lead gen is smaller. When benchmarking, segment by device-a blended rate masks performance problems on one platform."}]]}]
3e:["$","div","7",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How do you know if your conversion rate benchmark is outdated?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Industry benchmarks shift 2-4 times annually as competitive landscape changes. Use current-year data (last 6-12 months) from your vertical. If your data source doesn't specify publication date or sample size, treat it skeptically. Outdated benchmarks can lead to misaligned goals and missed optimization opportunities."}]]}]
